  "summary": "Admit explicit unstated valid time without inventing a timestamp or domain order.",
  "why": "Luis approved the missing-time Core follow-on after the completed structured-source and locator work. Decision 28 selects NONE_STATED with explicit null in the current private population/change-set grammar. KnowledgeValidTime.from_data replaces the duplicated parsers; the public Shop tests prove compilation, atomic admission, reopen, trace, separate explicit replacement and cross-kind refusal. INSTANT and ORDER_ONLY retain their meanings. The document adapter, domain profiles, root ontology, Assent time model and frozen evidence remain unchanged. RED 7 failed and 9 passed; focused GREEN 358 passed; cumulative compiler and Shop gate 715 passed with the same three pre-existing evidence-regeneration failures documented separately. No release, stable-wire, time-inference, generic temporal-query, paper-evaluation or model-ranking claim is made.",
